<article class="env-lemma" id="0DN5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DN5">Lemma <span data-tag="0DN5">101.25.6</span>.</a> Let $f : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ be a flat morphism of algebraic stacks. Let $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A) \to \mathcal{Y}$ be a morphism where $A$ is a valuation ring. If the closed point of $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ maps to a point of $|\mathcal{Y}|$ in the image of $|\mathcal{X|} \to |\mathcal{Y}|$, then there exists a commutative diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A') \ar[r] \ar[d] &  \mathcal{X} \ar[d] \\  \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A) \ar[r] &  \mathcal{Y} }  \]
</div>
  <p> where $A \to A'$ is an extension of valuation rings (More on Algebra, Definition <a href="/tag/0ASG" data-tag="0ASG">15.125.1</a>). </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The base change $\mathcal{X}_ A \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ is flat (Lemma <a href="/tag/06PY" data-tag="06PY">101.25.3</a>) and the closed point of $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ is in the image of $|\mathcal{X}_ A| \to |\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)|$ (Properties of Stacks, Lemma <a href="/tag/04XH" data-tag="04XH">100.4.3</a>). Thus we may assume $\mathcal{Y} = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$. Let $U \to \mathcal{X}$ be a surjective smooth morphism where $U$ is a scheme. Then we can apply Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/089F" data-tag="089F">67.42.4</a> to the morphism $U \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ to conclude. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>